  "contract_checks": [
    {
      "id": "IC01",
      "result": "pass_source_and_reused_test_evidence",
      "topic": "same_target_and_acceptance",
      "evidence": [
        "crates/vigilode-coupled/src/raw_step.rs:272",
        "crates/vigilode-coupled/src/raw_step.rs:605",
        "crates/vigilode-coupled/src/adaptive.rs:209"
      ],
      "detail": "The direct protected route and candidate fallback use the same protected workspace and original eight raw-U residuals. Candidate and protected results pass the same adaptive finite-value and effective-error <= 1 test. Accepted trajectory/history commit remains after output acceptance and model-epoch checks. This preserves existing acceptance contracts; it does not establish a global error estimator theorem."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC02",
      "result": "pass_source_and_reused_test_evidence",
      "topic": "fatal_callback_propagation",
      "evidence": [
        "crates/vigilode-coupled/src/raw_step.rs",
        "crates/vigilode-coupled/tests/switching_contracts.rs"
      ],
      "detail": "Guarded callbacks independently flag model errors before solver error classification, so a user callback that returns CoreError::LinearSolve cannot become a retryable trusted solver failure. Nonfinite callback output and model epoch mutation remain terminal. Focused test verifies one callback, one attempt and unchanged accepted state."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC03",
      "result": "pass_source_and_reused_test_evidence",
      "topic": "work_accounting",
      "detail": "Candidate callback work, protected workspace counters and separate original-residual validation are accumulated. Protected callback counters are replaced with actual guarded callback attempts, not added twice. The controller adds validation cost to protected cost; unit contract covers the overlapping-counter hazard. Atomic callback tests check both actual totals and zero candidate work during skips. Orthogonalization/vector/setup/time coverage is limited by the documented work proxy."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC04",
      "result": "pass_source",
      "topic": "no_oracle_routing",
      "detail": "CandidateRoute is caller declared. State decisions consume only prior protected work, current accepted/rejected status and current work receipts. Analytic references, model names, exact errors and benchmark winners never enter switching state. The registered uniform policy is not retrospectively fitted to individual case results."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC05",
      "result": "pass_source_and_reused_test_evidence",
      "topic": "cooldown_and_hysteresis",
      "detail": "Only accepted protected steps decrement cooldown. Ordinary local-error rejection does not mark a successfully solved candidate as a root failure. Candidate decline invokes immediate guarded fallback. Final priced cadence chooses L=clamp(ceil(C/(epsilon*P))-1,1,max_cooldown); legacy None retains exponential backoff. Successful re-entry resets backoff. P_probes <= 1 + floor(A/c) uses c=1 for priced mode and initial_cooldown for legacy mode. It is not a bound on total trajectory work or wall time."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC06",
      "result": "pass_manual_derivation",
      "topic": "benchmark_exact_solutions",
      "detail": "Checked initial conditions and derivatives for all seven model families: diagonal exponentials; unchanged synthetic-cost diagonal model; scalar Riccati y=a*y0*exp(a*t)/(a+0.5*y0*(1-exp(a*t))); triangular block y0=5*(exp(-t)-exp(-20*t))/19, y1=0.1*exp(-20*t); damped rotation exp(-0.1*t)*(cos(1000*t),sin(1000*t)); clock-augmented varying rate y=0.1*exp(-a*t-b*(1-exp(-40*t))/40). JVP clock derivative is +40*b*exp(-40*clock)*y. Ordinary floating-point evaluation is not interval certified."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC07",
      "result": "pass_source",
      "topic": "band_storage",
      "detail": "Benchmark uses row-major compact storage row*(lower+upper+1)+col+lower-row, consistent with the BandedJacobian contract. Oscillatory 2x2 blocks use lower=upper=1; triangular blocks use lower=0,upper=1; diagonal models use zero bandwidth. Clock-augmented global first column is excluded from compact-band arm."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC08",
      "result": "pass_with_scope_limits",
      "topic": "benchmark_fairness",
      "detail": "Primary experiment includes fixed/adaptive causal, same-target raw protected, fast matrix-free, dense and applicable banded controls; common observation schedule and physical error cap; failed/incomplete/inaccurate rows retained; one warmup and cyclic interleaving; complete per-solve workspace/probes/rejection/fallback/receipt allocation timed. Resource permissions differ explicitly (analytic dense/banded Jacobian versus supplied JVP). Root-variant extension must be interpreted jointly with primary banded controls, not as evidence of superiority over the fastest applicable structural solver."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC09",
      "result": "pass_source_and_reused_test_evidence",
      "topic": "priced_failed_exploration_round3",
      "detail": "The final rule uses actual candidate work C and successful same-attempt protected P, otherwise previous successful P; neither exact answers nor benchmark identities enter the choice. Code computes ceil((C/P)/epsilon)-1, clamps below at one and above at max_cooldown, records upper clipping, and leaves valid-but-expensive candidates on legacy exponential backoff. None reproduces the original failure cadence. Candidate or protected score overflow is explicitly nullable and flagged; invalid epsilon and nonfinite/negative input weights are refused."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC10",
      "result": "pass_conditional_real_arithmetic_derivation",
      "topic": "priced_cadence_bound_scope",
      "detail": "For representative fixed positive C,P, no upper clipping and exact real arithmetic, L+1 >= C/(epsilon*P), hence C/((L+1)P) <= epsilon. An accepted-step interpretation additionally requires the failed-probe attempt to have an accepted protected endpoint: it plus the next L accepted protected steps gives L+1. If that endpoint is rejected, only a prediction is valid; L accepted cooldown steps alone do not justify the L+1 accepted-progress denominator. Binary64 computations are estimates, not outward interval certificates. CAUSAL_SWITCH.md and README now state these conditions."
    },
    {
      "id": "IC11",
      "result": "pass_experiment_design_source",
      "topic": "legacy_and_persistent_failure_controls",
      "detail": "Final primary modes include legacy-switching-causal alongside fixed, priced and applicable protected solvers. The explicit --basis-limit setting creates a separately named stress case with actual small projection rank; it is caller-supplied and does not grant the controller case-name access. The stress case must remain separate from the original seven models and cannot support a general speed claim."
    }
  ],
