      "finding": "fallback_attempts includes intentional protected calibration/cooldown dispatch, not just failed candidate probes. candidate_skipped preserves the distinction; README already explains compatibility.",
      "recommendation": "In report tables call this protected-route attempts, or present a separate actual fallback count = fallback_attempted and not candidate_skipped. Do not infer root failure rate from this field alone.",
      "status": "documented_ensure_analysis_labels"
    },
    {
      "id": "IR03",
      "severity": "informational",
      "topic": "initial_protected_failure",
      "source": "crates/vigilode-coupled/src/switching.rs:166",
      "finding": "Calibration does not finish until a protected step is accepted, so a candidate is not a rescue for a trajectory whose initial protected route never succeeds.",
      "recommendation": "State this limitation. A future protected-failure rescue would need separately bounded eligibility, original-residual acceptance and fatal-error rules; do not silently add it to this experiment.",
      "status": "explicitly_documented_no_required_code_change"
    },
    {
      "id": "IR04",
      "severity": "informational",
      "topic": "reference_and_accuracy_scope",
      "source": "crates/vigilode-coupled/examples/reconsideration_bench.rs:240",
      "finding": "Eligibility is a predeclared sampled absolute-error cap of 1e-5 on 17 times. Scaled error is diagnostic, analytic references use ordinary f64, and continuous trajectory/reference uncertainty is not certified.",
      "recommendation": "Do not state rigorous global accuracy or all-tolerance superiority. Retain errors alongside speedups; test tighter tolerances and independent high precision before such claims.",
      "status": "disclosed_protocol_scope"
    },
    {
      "id": "IR05",
      "severity": "informational",
      "topic": "exit_code_is_not_numerical_pass",
      "source": "crates/vigilode-coupled/examples/reconsideration_bench.rs:278",
      "finding": "Campaign can exit zero after serializing individual failed solver rows.",
      "recommendation": "Aggregate success, completed observations, finite error and common error cap from each row; never use process exit alone as solver eligibility.",
      "status": "analysis_requirement"
    },
    {
      "id": "IR06",
      "severity": "informational",
      "topic": "work_proxy_staleness",
      "source": "crates/vigilode-coupled/src/switching.rs",
      "finding": "Protected EWMA may come from another state or h; default equal RHS/JVP cost omits machine-dependent vector/projection overhead and h-progress normalization.",
      "recommendation": "Present achieved wall time separately; do not infer regret/runtime guarantee. Future work may use h-normalized measured costs with explicit bounded exploration, not benchmark identities.",
      "status": "already_documented_and_stationary_bound_scoped"
    },
    {
      "id": "IR07",
      "severity": "informational",
